ent":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"code":"callback","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" must take a single argument of type "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/StringName","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" which will contain the type name of the selected object or be empty if no item is selected."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"code":"baseType","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" specifies the base type of objects to display. For example, if you set this to “Resource”, all types derived from "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Resource","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" will display in the create dialog."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"currentType"},{"text":" will be passed in the search box of the create dialog, and the specified type can be immediately selected when the dialog pops up. If the ","type":"text"},{"code":"currentType","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is not derived from ","type":"text"},{"code":"baseType","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", there will be no result of the type in the dialog."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"code":"dialogTitle","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" allows you to define a custom title for the dialog. This is useful if you want to accurately hint the usage of the dialog. If the "},{"code":"dialogTitle","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is an empty string, the dialog will use “Create New ‘Base Type’” as the default title.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"typeBlocklist"},{"type":"text","text":" contains a list of type names, and the types in the blocklist will be hidden from the